---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ACCURACY NOTE, READ BEFORE EDITING
//
// This policy describes what the site ACTUALLY does today. As of now that is:
//   - hosted on Netlify, which keeps standard server request logs
//   - a contact form handled by Netlify Forms
//   - one sessionStorage value for affiliate attribution
//   - NO analytics, NO ads, NO newsletter, NO embedded third-party content
//
// If you add any of those, update this page BEFORE the service goes live.
// A privacy policy that overstates what you collect is as much a problem as
// one that understates it, because it describes processing you cannot justify.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'hello@thegoodhomelist.online';
const updated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric',
});
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`What information ${SITE.name} collects, what it does not collect, how it is used, and the rights you have over it.`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]} />
    <article class="read prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This policy explains what information {SITE.name} collects when you visit
        {' '}<a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>, why, and what rights you
        have over it. It is written to describe what this site actually does, rather than to cover
        every possibility.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        We do not run analytics. We do not set cookies. We do not have accounts, a newsletter, or
        advertising. Unless you email us or use the contact form, we hold nothing that identifies
        you beyond the standard server logs our host keeps.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is operated by Rona Jane Sabatin. For any privacy question or request, email
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Server logs</h2>
      <p>
        This site is hosted by Netlify. Like any web host, Netlify records standard technical
        information when a page is requested: IP address, browser type, device type, the page
        requested, the referring page, and the time. These logs exist to serve the site, keep it
        secure and diagnose faults.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not use these logs to build a profile of you, and we do not combine them with
        anything else. Netlify processes them as our hosting provider under its own privacy terms.
      </p>

      <h2>The contact form</h2>
      <p>
        If you use the contact form, we receive the name, email address and message you enter.
        Submissions are handled by Netlify Forms and are visible to us in the Netlify dashboard.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use that information only to reply to you. We do not add you to a mailing list, and we
        do not pass it to anyone else. Messages are kept while the conversation is useful and
        deleted when it is not. You can ask us to delete yours sooner.
      </p>

      <h2>What we store in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        One value, in session storage, recording which affiliate tracking ID applies to your
        visit. It is deleted when you close the tab, is never sent to a server, and contains
        nothing that identifies you. The <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a> covers this
        in full.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        None currently. If we add analytics later, we will choose a privacy-conscious service that
        does not track individuals across sites, and we will update this page before it goes live.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links and Amazon</h2>
      <p>
        This site contains affiliate links. When you click one, you leave this site and the
        destination retailer records that you arrived from here so any purchase can be credited to
        us. That happens on their site, under their privacy policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        What we see in return is aggregate: a count of clicks, items ordered and commission earned.
        We do not receive your name, your email address, your payment details, or anything else
        that identifies you as an individual customer. Amazon does not share that with us.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our commercial relationship is described in the
        {' '}<a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we never do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Sell or rent personal information. We have none to sell</li>
        <li>Run advertising or retargeting</li>
        <li>Track you across other websites</li>
        <li>Create user accounts or profiles</li>
        <li>Use your contact message for marketing</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Legal basis for processing</h2>
      <p>
        For readers in the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom: server logs are
        processed on the basis of our legitimate interest in operating and securing the site.
        Contact form messages are processed on the basis of your consent, given by choosing to
        send us a message, and our legitimate interest in replying to you.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access the personal information we
        hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, object to how it is processed, or receive a
        copy of it. Readers in the EEA and UK have these rights under the GDPR. Readers in
        California have comparable rights under the CCPA and CPRA, including the right to know
        what is collected and the right to request deletion.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell or share personal information as those laws define it, so there is nothing
        to opt out of, but you are welcome to confirm that with us.
      </p>
      <p>
        To exercise any right, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We
        will respond within 30 days. We will not charge you or make you justify the request.
      </p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        The site is operated from the Philippines and hosted on infrastructure in the United
        States and elsewhere. If you are in the EEA or UK, your information may be processed
        outside your country. Where that happens, it is limited to the server logs and contact
        messages described above.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is intended for adults and is not directed at children under 13. We do not
        knowingly collect information from them. If you believe a child has sent us information,
        email us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served over HTTPS and is a static site, which means there is no database of
        visitor information to breach. No system is perfectly secure, but the most reliable
        protection is not holding data in the first place, and that is the approach here.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We will update this page if what we collect changes, with a revised date at the top. If a
        change is significant, we will say what changed rather than quietly editing the text.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>

      <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.9rem;margin-top:36px;">
        See also our <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a>,
        {' '}<a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> and
        {' '}<a href="/terms-and-conditions/">terms and conditions</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
